[{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Show that each of the following are divisible by 4.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2n+1)(2n-3)-4n+23\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16^{3k}-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2^{k+2}-4\\times3^k+8\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\" (2n+1)(2n-3)-4n+23=4n^2-4n-3-4n+23 \" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=4n^2-8n+20=4(n^2-2n+5)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore(2n+1)(2n-3)-4n+23\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"16^{3k}-4=(4^2)^{3k}-4=4^{6k}-4=4(4^{6k-1}-1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore16^{3k}-4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2^{k+2}-4\\times3^k+8=2^2\\times2^k-4\\times3^k+8=4(2^k-3^k+2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore2^{k+2}-4\\times3^k+8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Show that each of the following are divisible by 6.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6^{k+1}-18\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2^{k+1}\\times3^{k+2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k^2+1)(k-4)+10(k^2+k+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"6^{k+1}-18=6\\times6^k-18=6(6^k-3)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore6^{k+1}-18\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 6.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2^{k+1}\\times3^{k+2}=2\\times2^k\\times3\\times3^{k+1}=6(2^k\\times3^{k+1})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore2^{k+1}\\times3^{k+2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 6.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(k^2+1)(k-4)+10(k^2+k+1)=k^3-4k^2+k-4+10k^2+10k+10\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=k^3+6k^2+11k+6=(k+1)(k+2)(k+3),\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>which is 3 consecutive integers. At least one of these factors will be even so the expression is a multiple of 2. One of the factors will be a multiple of 3. As the expression is a multiple of both 2 and 3, it must be a multiple of 6. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore(k^2+1)(k-4)+10(k^2+k+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 6.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive integers, decide whether each of the following statements are true or false:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are factors of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a+b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a factor of both <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then both <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are factors of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>False: if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a+b=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which does not divide 6.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>True:<br>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"pa=b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"qa=c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for some values <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+c=pa+qa=a(p+q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>False: if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+c=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> but <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are not factors of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>True:<br>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"pa=b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"qb=c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for some values <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+c=pa+qb=pa+pqa=a(p+pq)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Prove, by induction, that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^2+n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 2 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1+1=1^2\\text{ which is divisible by 2 so true for }n=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k^2+k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 2.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(k+1)^2+(k+1)=k^2+2k+1+k+1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=k^2+3k+2=(k^2+k)+2k+2=(k^2+k)+2(k+1).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k^2+k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 2 and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2(k+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 2, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k^2+k)+2(k+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be divisible by 2.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Using proof by induction, prove that</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^3-n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 3</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^3+3n^2+2n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 6 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1-1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 3 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k^3-k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 3.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(k+1)^3-(k+1)=k^3+3k^2+3k+1-k-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=k^3+3k^2+2k=(k^3-k)+3k^2+3k=(k^3-k)+3(k^2+k).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k^3-k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 3 and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3(k^2+k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 3, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k^3-k)+3(k^2+k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be divisible by 3.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+3+2=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 6 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k^3+3k^2+2k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 6.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(k+1)^3+3(k+1)^2+2(k+1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=k^3+3k^2+3k+1+3k^2+6k+3+2k+2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=k^3+6k^2+11k+6=(k^3+3k^2+2k)+3k^2+9k+6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=(k^3-k)+3(k^2+3k+2)=(k^3-k)+3(k+1)(k+2).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k^3-k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 6, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k+2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are consecutive integers so one must be even so that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3(k+1)(k+2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be divisible by both 2 and 3 therefore divisible by 6. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k^3-k)+3(k+1)(k+2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be divisible by 6.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Prove, by induction, that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9^n+7\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 8 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9^1+7=16\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 8 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9^k+7\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 8.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"9^{k+1}+7=9\\times9^k+63-56=9(9^k+7)-56.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9^k+7\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 8 and 56 is divisible by 8 then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9(9^k+7)-56\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be divisible by 8.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Using proof by induction, prove that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^n-4n+3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^1-4+3=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 4 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^k-4k+3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5^{k+1}-4(k+1)+3=5\\times5^k-4k-1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=5\\times5^k-20k+15+16k-16=5(5^k-4k+3)+4(4k-4).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^k-4k+3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4 and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4(4k-4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4 then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5(5^k-4k+3)+4(4k-4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be divisible by 4.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Using proof by induction, prove that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^n+4n-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 8 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^1+4-1=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 8 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^k+4k-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 8.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5^{k+1}+4(k+1)-1=5\\times5^k+4k+3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=5\\times5^k+20k-5-16k+8=5(5^k+4k-1)-8(2k-1).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^k+4k-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 8 and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8(2k-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 8 then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5(5^k+4k-1)-8(2k-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be divisible by 8.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>Prove, by induction, that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6^n-2^n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 4 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6^1-2^1=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is a multiple of 4 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6^k-2^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 4.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"6^{k+1}-2^{k+1}=6\\times6^k-2\\times2^k\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=2\\times6^k+4\\times6^k-2\\times2^k=2(6^k-2^k)+4\\times6^k.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6^k-2^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 4 and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\times6^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 4 then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2(6^k-2^k)+4\\times6^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be a multiple of 4.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Prove, by induction, that</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^n+3\\times9^n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^{2n}+3^{2n-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^1+3\\times9^1=32\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 4 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^k+3\\times9^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5^{k+1}+3\\times9^{k+1}=5\\times5^k+3\\times9\\times9^k\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=5\\times5^k+27\\times9^k=5\\times5^k+15\\times9^k+12\\times9^k\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=5(5^k+3\\times9^k)+12\\times9^k.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^k+3\\times9^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4 and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\\times9^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4 then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5(5^k+3\\times9^k)+12\\times9^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be divisible by 4.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^2+3^{2-1}=28\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 4 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^{2k}+3^{2k-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5^{2(k+1)}+3^{2(k+1)-1}=5^{2k+2}+3^{2k+1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=25\\times5^{2k}+3^2\\times3^{2k-1}=25\\times5^{2k}+9\\times3^{2k-1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=25\\times5^{2k}+25\\times3^{2k-1}-16\\times3^{2k-1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=25(5^{2k}+3^{2k-1})-16\\times3^{2k-1}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5^{2k}+3^{2k-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4 and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16\\times3^{2k-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4 then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25(5^{2k}+3^{2k-1})-16\\times3^{2k-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be divisible by 4.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Prove, by induction, that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15^n-8^{n-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 7 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15^2-8^{2-2}=224\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 7 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15^k-8^{k-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 7.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"15^{k+1}-8^{k+1-2}=15\\times15^k-8\\times8^{k-2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=15\\times15^k-15\\times8^{k-2}+7\\times8^{k-2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=15(15^k-8^{k-2})+7\\times8^{k-2}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15^k-8^{k-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 7 and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7\\times8^{k-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 7 then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15(15^k-8^{k-2})+7\\times8^{k-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be divisible by 7.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Prove, using induction, that for all positive odd integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3^n+7^n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 10.</p>","steps":["<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3^1+7^1=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 10 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is odd: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3^k+7^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 10.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3^{k+2}+7^{k+2}=3^2\\times3^k+7^2\\times7^k\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=9(3^k+7^k)+40\\times7^k.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3^k+7^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 10 and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"40\\times7^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 10 then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9(3^k+7^k)+40\\times7^k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be divisible by 10.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is odd, then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all odd integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>The following shows a student’s answer to the question “Prove, by induction, that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3^{2n}-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 8 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>”.</p><blockquote><p>True for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span><br>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span><br><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3^{2(k+1)}-1)-(3^{2k}-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span><br><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=3^{2k}\\times3^2-3^{2k}=3^{2k}(9-1)=8\\times3^{2k}\" data-display=\"false\"></span><br>which is a multiple of 8 so true for all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></blockquote><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find all the errors.</p></li><li><p>Correct the proof.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Errors:<br>Didn’t check true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.<br>Didn’t state “assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>”.<br>Only attempted to show that the difference in two terms is divisible by 8 rather than specifically looking at the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> case.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(k)=3^{2k}-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3^2-1=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is a multiple of 8 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3^{2k}-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 8.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(k+1)-f(k)=(3^{2(k+1)}-1)-(3^{2k}-1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(k+1)-8m=3^2\\times3^{2k}-3^{2k}\\quad\\text{where }m\\text{ is some integer}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(k+1)=8m+(9-1)\\times3^{2k}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(k+1)=8m+8\\times3^{2k}=8[m+3^{2k}],\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>which is divisible by 8.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>Prove by induction that the sum of the cubes of three consecutive positive integers is divisible by 3.</p>","steps":["<p>Let three consecutive positive integers be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> therefore proving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n^3+(n+1)^3+(n+2)^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 3.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1^3+2^3+3^3=36\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 3 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k^3+(k+1)^3+(k+2)^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 3.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(k+1)^3+(k+2)^3+(k+3)^3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=k^3+3k^2+3k+1+k^3+6k^2+12k+8+k^3+9k^2+27k+27\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=3k^3+18k^2+42k+36=3[k^3+6k^2+14k+12],\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>which is divisible by 3.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, it is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(n)=50n^2+70n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(n+1)-f(n)=20(5n+6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence prove by induction that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 4 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(n+1)-f(n)=50(n+1)^2+70(n+1)-(50n^2+70n)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=50n^2+100n+50+70n+70-50n^2-70n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=100n+120=20(5n+6)\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(1)=50+70=120\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 4 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: so let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(k)=4m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for some integer <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(k+1)-f(k)=20(5k+6)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(k+1)-4m=20(5k+6)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(k+1)=4m+20(5k+6)=4[m+5(5k+6)],\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>which is divisible by 4.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, it is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(n)=24\\times2^{4n}+3^{4n}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(n+1)-f(n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence prove by induction that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is divisible by 5 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(n+1)-f(n)=24\\times2^{4(n+1)}+3^{4(n+1)}-24\\times2^{4n}-3^{4n}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=24\\times2^{4n+4}+3^{4n+4}-24\\times2^{4n}-3^{4n}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=384\\times2^{4n}+81\\times3^{4n}-24\\times2^{4n}-3^{4n}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=360\\times2^{4n}+80\\times3^{4n}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(1)=24\\times2^4+3^4=465\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is divisible by 5 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: so let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(k)=5m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for some integer <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(k+1)-f(k)=360\\times2^{4k}+80\\times3^{4k}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(k+1)-5m=360\\times2^{4k}+80\\times3^{4k}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(k+1)=5m+360\\times2^{4k}+80\\times3^{4k}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(k+1)=5[m+72\\times2^{4k}+16\\times3^{4k}],\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>which is divisible by 5.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.47-q17","number":17,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Prove that for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(n)=2n^3-5n\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 3.</p></li><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(-x)=-f(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for all real values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence prove that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 3 for all integer values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2-5=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is a multiple of 3 so true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Assume true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k^3-5k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 3.</p>","<p>Prove true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2(k+1)^3-5(k+1)=2k^3+6k^2+6k+2-5k-5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=2k^3+6k^2+k-3=(2k^3-5k)+6k^2+6k-3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"=(2k^3-5k)+3(2k^2+2k-1).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since we assumed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k^3-5k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 3 and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3(2k^2+2k-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 3, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2k^3-5k)+3(2k^2+2k-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be a multiple of 3.</p>","<p>As the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and if the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> then the statement is true for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n=k+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the statement is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(-x)=2(-x)^3-5(-x)=-2x^3+5x=-(2x^3-5x)=-f(x).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>From part a), <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 3 for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\ge1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. From part b), <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(-n)=-f(n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so is a multiple of 3 so is true for all integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\le1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(0)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which is a multiple of 3. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore f(n)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a multiple of 3 for all integer values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]}]